usage: test_kernel_axiom_audit.py [-h] [--output OUTPUT]

Replay the real Lean axiom command against isolated imported fixture modules.
Run from any directory. Outputs, copied audit source, fixtures, command
records, tool identity, and source hashes go to a new directory outside the
repository. Exit 0 means every behavioral assertion passed; exit 1 means a
test failed. An invocation/setup error exits 3. Lean itself uses exit 1 for
both forbidden axioms and empty scope; tests distinguish their exact
diagnostics.

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT  new evidence directory outside the repository
